/*

Signal model for the libsignal integration: PQXDH (pqxdh.owl) followed by the
double ratchet (double_ratchet.owl). full.owl checks both. Derived from
tests/wip/signal/pqxdh_double_ratchet; the differences are the def boundaries and the concrete
formats (see INTERFACE below).

The two protocols share one KDF scope, because Signal's key schedule is one
KDF chain: X3DH's master key RK_0 salts Alice's initial ratchet step LA_init,
whose root key RK_1 salts Bob's first step LB<0>.

CONCRETE FORMATS (libsignal v0.103, SPQR disabled)

  - master key (PQXDH): HKDF(salt = 0x, ikm = 0xFF*32 || DH1 || DH2 || DH3
    || DH4 || SS, info = "WhisperText_X25519_SHA-256_CRYSTALS-KYBER-1024")
    = RK_0 || CK_0, where SS is the shared secret of Alice's encapsulation to
    Bob's signed Kyber prekey pqbo. Every rule of the key schedule takes SS
    as its parameter k (see the PQXDH notes below).
    CK_0 is the chain key libsignal stores for Bob's signed prekey; no
    message is ever sent under it, so it is a public output here.
  - ratchet steps: HKDF(salt = RK, ikm = DH, info = "WhisperRatchet")
    = RK' || CK.
  - messages: the st_aead key is the chain key CK. Concretely st_aead is
    libsignal's message encryption (trusted, in execlib): message keys from
    HMAC(CK, 0x01) and HKDF "WhisperMessageKeys", AES-256-CBC, and an
    8-byte HMAC-SHA256 tag over the AAD and the ciphertext.
  - AAD = IK_sender || IK_receiver || ratchet key || counter (8) ||
    previous counter (8) [|| addresses]. The trusted AEAD encodes it as
    libsignal's MAC input (33-byte keys, protobuf header).
  - Lockstep only: one message per chain, so counter = previous counter = 0.

INTERFACE (one def per libsignal event; see pqxdh.owl, double_ratchet.owl)

  Alice: alice_init          (process_prekey_bundle: X3DH, LA_init)
         alice_send_init     (first message_encrypt: the PreKeySignalMessage)
         alice_recv_0        (decrypt Bob's first message, her step LA<0>)
         alice_recv_succ<i>  (decrypt, her step LA<succ(i)>)
         alice_send<i>       (encrypt under LA<i>)
  Bob:   bob_recv_prekey     (process_prekey + decrypt: X3DH, LA_init, his step LB<0>)
         bob_recv_1          (decrypt Alice's round-0 reply, his step LB<1>)
         bob_recv_succ<i>    (decrypt, his step LB<succ(succ(i))>)
         bob_send<i>         (encrypt under LB<i>)

Ratchet keys are fresh per step and are passed in as def parameters of type
Name(a<..>) / Name(b<..>): OwlC erases indices, so they cannot be cfg names.
The application must generate each one fresh and never reuse it. A party's
current ratchet key is kept in its state struct.

PQXDH (as in tests/wip/signal/pqxdh_double_ratchet)

  The KEM shared secret of the handshake is a rule parameter k (L1(k),
  LA_init(k), LB<i>(k), ...), not an index: the index of kem_encaps is
  ghost, and defs cannot take ghost indices. An instance is applicable when
  some DH atom has both keys secret or when k is a secret shared secret
  KEMName<pqbo, i>. Every def and state carries the KEM secret as a ghost
  (kss). Because k is free, a public root key could equal the corrupt root
  key of another k; the public branch of each double ratchet state therefore
  carries no_chain_b<i> / no_chain_a<i> (it is the root key of that round for
  no KEM secret), proved from the X3DH input by collision resistance.

  Signed prekeys: as in PQXDH, long_sskB signs Encode(PK), a key type byte
  followed by the key: 0x05 ++ dhpk(bs) and 0x08 ++ kem_pk(pqbo). These are
  libsignal's serialized forms of the signed prekey and of a Kyber1024
  prekey (kem_pk is the raw encapsulation key). The tags keep the two signed
  keys apart without a length assumption on kem_pk; the verified path only
  takes Kyber1024 prekeys (libsignal's KEM, KeyType::Kyber1024).

*/

locality alice
locality bob

// X3DH: Alice's initial message
counter N_c @ alice
counter N_c_bob_init @ bob
// Double ratchet
counter N_c_alice @ alice
counter N_c_bob   @ bob

// ---------- NAMES OUTSIDE THE KDF SCOPE --------------------------------------

name ma1 : nonce @ alice // Alice's initial message (X3DH)

// Double ratchet plaintext secrets, one per round and direction. mb<0> is
// Bob's first ratchet message, sent in reply to the X3DH handshake.
name mb<i> : nonce @ bob    // Bob's message in round i
name ma<i> : nonce @ alice  // Alice's message in round i

// ---------- EVENTS ------------------------------------------------------------

// Alice records the plaintext, the DH input and the AAD of her initial message.
def event_alice_send_msg1 @ alice
def event_bob_recv_msg1 @ bob

// The sender records its plaintext before encrypting; the receiver asserts
// the event after a successful decryption.
def bob_sent<i> @ bob
def alice_sent<i> @ alice

kdf_scope Signal {

    // ---------- X3DH -----------------------------------------------------------

    // Alice's DH keys
    name long_skA : DH @ alice // Alice's identity key
    name ae1 : DH @ alice      // Alice's base (ephemeral) key, one per session

    // Bob's DH keys
    name long_skB : DH @ bob   // Bob's identity key
    name bs : DH @ bob         // Bob's signed prekey
    name bo : DH @ bob         // Bob's one-time prekey
    // Bob's signed Kyber prekey (PQXDH). Its shared secrets KEMName<pqbo, i>,
    // one per encapsulation i, are KDF keys of this scope.
    name pqbo : kemkey (kdfkey) @ bob

    // ---------- DOUBLE RATCHET ---------------------------------------------------

    // Ratchet DH keys. a<0> is Alice's ratchet key in the X3DH initial
    // message; a<succ(i)> is generated by Alice in round i, b<i> by Bob in
    // round i.
    name a<i> : DH @ alice
    name b<i> : DH @ bob

    // ---------- X3DH HELPER FUNCTIONS AND PREDICATES ---------------------------

    // The PQXDH ikm, including libsignal's 32 0xFF "discontinuity bytes";
    // k is the KEM shared secret.
    func correct_amaster_arg(k) =
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(long_skA))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(long_skB)), get(ae1))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(ae1))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bo)), get(ae1))
        ++ k

    func correct_bmaster_arg(k) =
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(long_skA)), get(bs))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(ae1)), get(long_skB))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(ae1)), get(bs))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(ae1)), get(bo))
        ++ k

    // The ikm without the KEM secret (for its length)
    func x3dh_dh() =
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(long_skA))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(long_skB)), get(ae1))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(ae1))
        ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bo)), get(ae1))

    // (The KEM secret is not in the secrecy condition, as in the PQXDH model.)
    predicate bob_good(dh, k) =
      dh == correct_bmaster_arg(k)
      /\
      // the adversary cannot compute the master secret iff some DH pair has
      // both keys secret
      ((sec(bs) /\ sec(long_skA)) \/ (sec(long_skB) /\ sec(ae1))
        \/ (sec(bs) /\ sec(ae1)) \/ (sec(bo) /\ sec(ae1)))

    // AEAD nametype for Alice's initial message. The AAD predicate records
    // agreement on the plaintext, on the X3DH DH input and on the whole AAD
    // (identity keys, Alice's ratchet key a<0>, counters, addresses).
    nametype ma1_enc(dh) = st_aead Name(ma1)
          aad x. happened(event_alice_send_msg1(get(ma1), dh, x))
          nonce N_c

    // ODH rule for the master key derivation. Output 0 is RK_0; output 1 is
    // CK_0 (unused, see CONCRETE FORMATS).
    odh L1(k) : 0x,
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_ss(bs, long_skA) ++ dh_ss(long_skB, ae1) ++ dh_ss(bs, ae1) ++ dh_ss(bo, ae1) ++ k,
        0x57686973706572546578745f5832353531395f5348412d3235365f4352595354414c532d4b594245522d31303234
        -> strict kdfkey || public kdfkey
    // Off-chain rules. A rule instance applies only when some honest DH
    // atom of its ikm has both keys secret, or k is a secret KEM secret; the
    // checker adds that condition itself. Otherwise every atom is adversary-computable, the call is out
    // of bounds of every rule, and the checker types it public.
    //
    // Alice with a forged one-time prekey y (honest s1, s2, s3).
    odh L1_badA(y, k) where
        (is_group_elem(y) /\ y != dhpk(get(bo)))
      : 0x,
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_ss(bs, long_skA) ++ dh_ss(long_skB, ae1) ++ dh_ss(bs, ae1) ++ dh_combine(y, get(ae1)) ++ k,
        0x57686973706572546578745f5832353531395f5348412d3235365f4352595354414c532d4b594245522d31303234
        -> strict kdfkey || public kdfkey
    // Bob with a forged ephemeral x for Alice (honest s1).
    odh L1_badB(x, k) where
        (is_group_elem(x) /\ x != dhpk(get(ae1)))
      : 0x,
        0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff
        ++ dh_ss(bs, long_skA) ++ dh_combine(x, get(long_skB)) ++ dh_combine(x, get(bs)) ++ dh_combine(x, get(bo)) ++ k,
        0x57686973706572546578745f5832353531395f5348412d3235365f4352595354414c532d4b594245522d31303234
        -> strict kdfkey || public kdfkey

    // AEAD nametype for a key that no honest party encrypts under (derived
    // by a _bad rule from a forged ratchet key): decryption can only fail.
    nametype ma1_corr = st_aead (y:Name(ma1){False})
          aad x. true
          nonce N_c

    // Alice's initial ratchet step ([DR] 3.3, 7.1): RK_1 || CK_A =
    // KDF_RK(RK_0, DH(a<0>, bs)). Bob's signed prekey bs is his initial
    // ratchet key, so bs occurs in two ODH rules (L1 and LA_init); the rules
    // are disjoint by salt (0x versus RK_0). Output 0 is RK_1, the root key
    // that enters the double ratchet (salt of Bob's first step LB<0>);
    // output 1 is the chain key of Alice's initial message.
    odh LA_init(k) : KDF<L1(k); kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>, dh_ss(a<0>, bs), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma1_enc(correct_amaster_arg(k))
    // Alice with a forged one-time prekey y (RK_0 from L1_badA).
    odh LA_init_badA(y, k) where
        (is_group_elem(y) /\ y != dhpk(get(bo)))
      : KDF<L1_badA(y, k); kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>, dh_ss(a<0>, bs), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey
        || strict ma1_enc(0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(long_skA)) ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(long_skB)), get(ae1)) ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(ae1)) ++ dh_combine(y, get(ae1)) ++ k)
    // Bob with a forged ephemeral x for Alice (RK_0 from L1_badB) and Alice's
    // honest ratchet key. Alice never derives this key (her L1 instances
    // contain dh(long_skB, ae1), this one dh(x, long_skB) with x != dhpk(ae1)),
    // so no honest party encrypts under it and a successful decryption is
    // contradictory. (The original model instead got the contradiction from
    // Alice's base key in the AAD; libsignal's MAC does not cover the base key.)
    odh LA_init_badB(x, k) where
        (is_group_elem(x) /\ x != dhpk(get(ae1)))
      : KDF<L1_badB(x, k); kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>, dh_ss(a<0>, bs), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma1_corr
    // Bob with a forged ratchet key z for Alice (honest RK_0).
    odh LA_init_badR(z, k) where
        (is_group_elem(z) /\ z != dhpk(get(a<0>)))
      : KDF<L1(k); kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>, dh_combine(z, get(bs)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma1_corr
    // Bob with a forged ephemeral x and a forged ratchet key z. Needed so
    // that, when RK_0 is a secret off-chain name (honest bs and long_skA),
    // Bob's key is a name no honest party encrypts under and a successful
    // decryption is contradictory.
    odh LA_init_badBR(x, z, k) where
        (is_group_elem(x) /\ x != dhpk(get(ae1)) /\ is_group_elem(z) /\ z != dhpk(get(a<0>)))
      : KDF<L1_badB(x, k); kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>, dh_combine(z, get(bs)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma1_corr

    // ---------- DOUBLE RATCHET RULES -------------------------------------------

    // AEAD nametypes for Bob's round-i message. AAD: IK_B || IK_A || his
    // ratchet key || counter 0 || previous counter 0.
    nametype mb_enc<i> = st_aead (m:Name(mb<i>){happened(bob_sent<i>(m))})
          aad x. (x == dhpk(get(long_skB)) ++ dhpk(get(long_skA)) ++ dhpk(get(b<i>))
                       ++ 0x00000000000000000000000000000000)
          nonce N_c_bob
    nametype mb_corr<i> = st_aead (y:Name(mb<i>){False})
          aad x. true
          nonce N_c_bob

    // AEAD nametypes for Alice's round-i message (carries her next key).
    // AAD: IK_A || IK_B || her ratchet key a<succ(i)> || 0 || 0.
    nametype ma_enc<i> = st_aead (m:Name(ma<i>){happened(alice_sent<i>(m))})
          aad x. (x == dhpk(get(long_skA)) ++ dhpk(get(long_skB)) ++ dhpk(get(a<succ(i)>))
                       ++ 0x00000000000000000000000000000000)
          nonce N_c_alice
    nametype ma_corr<i> = st_aead (y:Name(ma<i>){False})
          aad x. true
          nonce N_c_alice

    // Bob's step ([DR] 3.5). Output 0 = root key; 1 = Bob's chain key.
    // Round 0 is salted by X3DH's root key RK_1 (rule LA_init) and uses
    // Alice's X3DH ratchet key a<0>.
    rec_odh<i> LB<i>(k)
        | 0        : KDF<LA_init(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>, dh_ss(a<0>, b<0>), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        | succ(i') : KDF<LA<i'>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,  dh_ss(a<i>, b<i>), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict mb_enc<i>

    rec_odh<i> LB_bad<i>(s, k) where (s != dh_combine(dhpk(get(a<i>)), get(b<i>)))
        | 0        : KDF<LA_init(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>, s, 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        | succ(i') : KDF<LA<i'>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,  s, 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict mb_corr<i>

    // Alice's step. Output 0 = root key; 1 = Alice's chain key.
    // Her fresh key in round i is a<succ(i)>; a<succ(i')> = a<i> is the key
    // Bob already used in LB<i>. LA never uses i': its salt LB<i> is from the
    // same round, so both cases have the same form.
    rec_odh<i> LA<i>(k)
        | 0        : KDF<LB<0>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,   dh_ss(a<succ(0)>, b<0>), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        | succ(i') : KDF<LB<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,   dh_ss(a<succ(i)>, b<i>), 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma_enc<i>

    rec_odh<i> LA_bad<i>(s, k) where (s != dh_combine(dhpk(get(a<succ(i)>)), get(b<i>)))
        | 0        : KDF<LB<0>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,   s, 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        | succ(i') : KDF<LB<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>,   s, 0x5768697370657252617463686574
        -> strict kdfkey || strict ma_corr<i>
}

// Bob's signing key (signs Encode(PK) of bs and pqbo for the prekey bundle;
// see the header). In Signal,
// long_sskB and long_skB are the SAME Curve25519 key (XEdDSA for signing,
// X25519 for DH), so their corruption is linked below.
name long_sskB : sigkey(x:Data<adv>{x == 0x05 ++ dhpk(get(bs)) \/ x == 0x08 ++ kem_pk(get(pqbo))}) @ bob

// ---------- CORRUPTION ASSUMPTIONS --------------------------------------------

// ae1 is unsigned in the handshake. Impersonation of Alice with a stolen
// long_skA is handled on Bob's side by the split on a1 == dhpk(get(ae1)) and
// the L1_badB rules, not by a flow corr [long_skA] ==> [ae1].
corr [long_sskB] ==> [long_skB]
corr [long_skB] ==> [long_sskB]

// No other corr flows. Plaintexts are parameters of the send defs, secret
// only when the sender holds the honest, secret key, so no plaintext name
// needs a flow; the labels of RK_1 and of every ratchet chain key follow
// from the applicability of their rule instances.

// ---------- WIRE STRUCTS ------------------------------------------------------
// Parsed and serialized by trusted protobuf shims (OwlC --no-vest).

// libsignal's SignalMessage: version byte || protobuf || 8-byte MAC.
// _sm_ctxt is the st_aead output (AES-CBC ciphertext || MAC); the shim puts
// the MAC after the protobuf. _sm_addr: sender and recipient addresses
// (36 bytes) or empty.
struct signal_message {
  _sm_rk   : Data<adv> ||group||,
  _sm_ctr  : Data<adv> ||counter||,
  _sm_prev : Data<adv> ||counter||,
  _sm_ctxt : Data<adv>,
  _sm_addr : Data<adv>
}

// libsignal's PreKeySignalMessage: version byte || protobuf. _pm_meta is an
// opaque encoding of the registration id and the prekey ids; _pm_kct is the
// Kyber ciphertext; _pm_msg is a serialized signal_message.
struct prekey_msg {
  _pm_meta : Data<adv>,
  _pm_kct  : Data<adv>,
  _pm_base : Data<adv> ||group||,
  _pm_ik   : Data<adv> ||group||,
  _pm_msg  : Data<adv>
}

// ---------- X3DH STATE ----------------------------------------------------------

// Alice's state after alice_init (for alice_send_init and alice_recv_0).
//   kss     : the KEM shared secret of her encapsulation (ghost).
//   apre    : her PQXDH input without the KEM secret (ghost).
//   adh, am : her PQXDH input and master key RK_0 (ghost).
//   ags     : Bob's signed prekey as she received it (ghost).
//   ra_y    : the one-time prekey she used (ghost).
//   ra      : her root key RK_1: the honest KDF<LA_init(kss);..;0>, the
//             off-chain root key of a session with a forged one-time prekey
//             (LA_init_badA), or public, with its provenance.
//   ka      : her initial chain key, of the same three kinds.
//   ak0     : her ratchet key a<0>.
//   gbs     : Bob's signed prekey (his first ratchet key), public.
//   ck0     : CK_0, for libsignal's session record (public).
//   kct     : the KEM ciphertext, for her PreKeySignalMessages.
//   b3      : Bob's identity key.
struct alice_init_state {
  ai_kss  : Ghost,
  ai_apre : (x:Ghost{ length(x) == length(x3dh_dh()) }),
  ai_adh  : (x:Ghost{ x == ai_apre ++ ai_kss }),
  ai_am   : (x:Ghost{ x == gkdf<kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>(0x, ai_adh,
                0x57686973706572546578745f5832353531395f5348412d3235365f4352595354414c532d4b594245522d31303234) }),
  ai_ags  : Ghost,
  ai_ra_y : Ghost,
  ai_ra_g : Ghost,
  ai_ra   : if ai_ra_g == get(KDF<LA_init(ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) then Name(KDF<LA_init(ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
            else if is_group_elem(ai_ra_y) /\ ai_ra_y != dhpk(get(bo))
                    /\ ai_ra_g == get(KDF<LA_init_badA(ai_ra_y, ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
            then Name(KDF<LA_init_badA(ai_ra_y, ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
            else (x:Data<adv> ||kdfkey||{ x == ai_ra_g /\
                    x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(ai_am, dh_combine(ai_ags, get(a<0>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574) }),
  ai_ka_g : (x:Ghost{
              (x == get(KDF<LA_init(ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) ==> ai_adh == correct_amaster_arg(ai_kss))
              /\ ((is_group_elem(ai_ra_y) /\ ai_ra_y != dhpk(get(bo))
                   /\ x == get(KDF<LA_init_badA(ai_ra_y, ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>))
                  ==> ai_adh == 0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(long_skA)) ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(long_skB)), get(ae1))
                               ++ dh_combine(dhpk(get(bs)), get(ae1)) ++ dh_combine(ai_ra_y, get(ae1)) ++ ai_kss) }),
  ai_ka   : if ai_ka_g == get(KDF<LA_init(ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LA_init(ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
            else if is_group_elem(ai_ra_y) /\ ai_ra_y != dhpk(get(bo))
                    /\ ai_ka_g == get(KDF<LA_init_badA(ai_ra_y, ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
            then Name(KDF<LA_init_badA(ai_ra_y, ai_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
            else Data<adv> ||enckey||,
  ai_ak0  : Name(a<0>),
  ai_gbs  : Data<adv> ||group||,
  ai_ck0  : Data<adv> ||kdfkey||,
  ai_kct  : Data<adv> ||kem_cipherlen||,
  ai_b3   : dhpk(long_skB)
}

// ---------- PREDICATES --------------------------------------------------------

// The root key after Bob's / Alice's step of round i is secret
predicate chain_b<i>(k) = sec(KDF<LB<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
predicate chain_a<i>(k) = sec(KDF<LA<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)

// x is the root key of round i for no KEM secret. The public state of the
// double ratchet satisfies this, which pins the KEM secret of its chain.
predicate no_chain_b<i>(x) = forall k:bv. x != get(KDF<LB<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
predicate no_chain_a<i>(x) = forall k:bv. x != get(KDF<LA<i>(k); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)

// ---------- DOUBLE RATCHET STATE ----------------------------------------------

// The double ratchet defs are state transformers: a receive def takes its
// state and returns the state for the next receive def, the chain key for
// the matching send def, and the decrypted plaintext. An application drives
// the rounds. Each state holds the KEM secret of the handshake (ghost), a
// party's root key after its own step, either the honest chain name or public
// with its gkdf provenance, split on a ghost copy (ra_g, rb_g), and the
// party's current ratchet key. A public root key is the root key of that
// round for no KEM secret (no_chain_a / no_chain_b).

// Alice's state before her receive def of round succ(i): her root key after
// her step LA<i>, and her ratchet key a<succ(i)>.
struct alice_state<i> {
  as_kss: Ghost,
  as_wpk: (x:Data<adv> ||group||{ is_group_elem(x) }),
  as_wsalt2: Ghost,
  as_ra_g: Ghost,
  as_wsalt: (x:Ghost{ as_ra_g != get(KDF<LA<i>(as_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) ==>
                      x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(as_wsalt2, dh_combine(as_wpk, get(a<i>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574) }),
  as_ra: if as_ra_g == get(KDF<LA<i>(as_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) then Name(KDF<LA<i>(as_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
         else (x:Data<adv> ||kdfkey||
               { x == as_ra_g /\ x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(as_wsalt, dh_combine(as_wpk, get(a<succ(i)>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574)
                 /\ no_chain_a<i>[x] }),
  as_ak: Name(a<succ(i)>),
  as_b3: dhpk(long_skB)
}

// Result of Alice's receive def of round i: her state after her step LA<i>,
// the chain key of LA<i> (for alice_send<i>), and Bob's round-i plaintext.
struct alice_recv_out<i> {
  aro_state: alice_state<idx i>,
  aro_kss: Ghost,
  aro_ka_g: Ghost,
  aro_ka: if aro_ka_g == get(KDF<LA<i>(aro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LA<i>(aro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
          else Data<adv> ||enckey||,
  aro_msg: Data<adv /\ [mb<i>], |adv|>,
  // Bob's chain key of LB<i>, which decrypted aro_msg (for libsignal's
  // receiver chain, used when Bob sends more than one message in the chain).
  aro_kb_g: Ghost,
  aro_kb: if aro_kb_g == get(KDF<LB<i>(aro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LB<i>(aro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
          else Data<adv> ||enckey||
}

// Bob's state before bob_recv_1: his root key after his step LB<0>, over the
// root key wsalt, and his ratchet key b<0>.
struct bob_state_1 {
  bs1_kss: Ghost,
  bs1_wpk: (x:Data<adv> ||group||{ is_group_elem(x) }),
  bs1_wsalt: Ghost,
  bs1_rb_g: Ghost,
  bs1_rb: if bs1_rb_g == get(KDF<LB<0>(bs1_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) then Name(KDF<LB<0>(bs1_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
          else (x:Data<adv> ||kdfkey||
                { x == bs1_rb_g /\ x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(bs1_wsalt, dh_combine(bs1_wpk, get(b<0>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574)
                  /\ no_chain_b<0>[x] }),
  bs1_bk: Name(b<0>),
  bs1_a3: dhpk(long_skA)
}

// Bob's state before his receive def of round succ(i): his root key after
// his step LB<succ(i)>, and his ratchet key b<succ(i)>.
struct bob_state<i> {
  bst_kss: Ghost,
  bst_wpk: (x:Data<adv> ||group||{ is_group_elem(x) }),
  bst_wsalt2: Ghost,
  bst_rb_g: Ghost,
  bst_wsalt: (x:Ghost{ bst_rb_g != get(KDF<LB<succ(i)>(bst_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) ==>
                       x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(bst_wsalt2, dh_combine(bst_wpk, get(b<i>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574) }),
  bst_rb: if bst_rb_g == get(KDF<LB<succ(i)>(bst_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) then Name(KDF<LB<succ(i)>(bst_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
          else (x:Data<adv> ||kdfkey||
                { x == bst_rb_g /\ x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(bst_wsalt, dh_combine(bst_wpk, get(b<succ(i)>)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574)
                  /\ no_chain_b<succ(i)>[x] }),
  bst_bk: Name(b<succ(i)>),
  bst_a3: dhpk(long_skA)
}

// Result of Bob's receive def of round i (bob_recv_1 for i = 0): his state
// after his step LB<succ(i)>, the chain key of LB<succ(i)> (for
// bob_send<succ(i)>), and Alice's round-i plaintext.
struct bob_recv_out<i> {
  bro_state: bob_state<idx i>,
  bro_kss: Ghost,
  bro_kb_g: Ghost,
  bro_kb: if bro_kb_g == get(KDF<LB<succ(i)>(bro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LB<succ(i)>(bro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
          else Data<adv> ||enckey||,
  bro_msg: Data<adv /\ [ma<i>], |adv|>,
  // Alice's chain key of LA<i>, which decrypted bro_msg (for libsignal's
  // receiver chain).
  bro_ka_g: Ghost,
  bro_ka: if bro_ka_g == get(KDF<LA<i>(bro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LA<i>(bro_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
          else Data<adv> ||enckey||
}

// Result of bob_recv_prekey: Bob's state for bob_recv_1, his chain key for
// bob_send<0>, and Alice's initial plaintext.
struct bob_prekey_out {
  bpo_state : bob_state_1,
  bpo_kss   : Ghost,
  bpo_kb_g  : Ghost,
  bpo_kb    : if bpo_kb_g == get(KDF<LB<0>(bpo_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LB<0>(bpo_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
              else Data<adv> ||enckey||,
  bpo_msg   : Data<adv /\ [ma1], |adv|>,
  // Alice's initial chain key, which decrypted bpo_msg (for libsignal's
  // receiver chain).
  bpo_ka_g  : Ghost,
  bpo_ka    : if bpo_ka_g == get(KDF<LA_init(bpo_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LA_init(bpo_kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
              else Data<adv> ||enckey||
}

// ---------- INTERFACE: X3DH -> DOUBLE RATCHET ---------------------------------

// Bob's first ratchet step LB<0>, called by bob_recv_prekey after it has
// decrypted Alice's initial message. Returns his state for bob_recv_1 and
// the chain key for bob_send<0>.
//   kss      : the KEM shared secret (ghost).
//   bpre     : Bob's PQXDH input without the KEM secret (ghost).
//   bdh, bm  : Bob's PQXDH input and master key RK_0 (ghost).
//   rb_g, rb : Bob's root key RK_1 = KDF_RK(RK_0, DH(gae, bs)). It is the
//              honest root key KDF<LA_init(kss);..;0> when that key is
//              secret; otherwise it is public, with this provenance.
//   gae      : Alice's ratchet key as Bob received it. It is her honest
//              a<0> whenever Bob holds the honest secret root key.
//   bk0      : Bob's fresh ratchet key b<0>.
def bob_step_0(
  kss: Ghost,
  bpre: (x:Ghost{ length(x) == length(x3dh_dh()) }),
  bdh: (x:Ghost{ x == bpre ++ kss }),
  bm: (x:Ghost{ x == gkdf<kdfkey || kdfkey; 0>(0x, bdh,
          0x57686973706572546578745f5832353531395f5348412d3235365f4352595354414c532d4b594245522d31303234) }),
  rb_g: Ghost,
  gae: (x:Data<adv> ||group||{
          (rb_g == get(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) /\ sec(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>))
            ==> x == dhpk(get(a<0>)) }),
  rb: if rb_g == get(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>) /\ sec(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
      then Name(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 0>)
      else (x:Data<adv> ||kdfkey||{ x == rb_g /\ x == gkdf<kdfkey || enckey; 0>(bm, dh_combine(gae, get(bs)), 0x5768697370657252617463686574) }),
  a3: dhpk(long_skA),
  bk0: Name(b<0>),
  ka_g: Ghost,
  ka: if ka_g == get(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>) then Name(KDF<LA_init(kss); kdfkey || enckey; 1>)
      else Data<adv> ||enckey||,
  pt: Data<adv /\ [ma1], |adv|>
) @ bob: Option bob_prekey_out
